      "message": "(Qwen + QLM 5.3)\n\n### 🟡 `--log-file` is opened twice (FILE* leak)\n\n`get_command_options()` is called twice — before and after `rbh_apply_aliases()` (pre-existing design, harmless for the old string/bool options). For the new `--log-file`, both passes call `fopen(..., \"w\")`: the first `FILE*` leaks and the file is re-truncated. Output is still correct (second handle writes everything), so this is a leak-once-per-run nit, but it\u0027s the first option in this parser that isn\u0027t idempotent. Same issue in report (commit 6 below).",
